{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Pre-Launch Readiness Audit",
  "description": "Comprehensive pre-launch validation that verifies core user journeys, authentication flows, critical APIs, test coverage, database migrations, observability setup, and deployment readiness. Generates a detailed launch checklist with status indicators and actionable recommendations.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Execute a comprehensive pre-launch readiness audit for the Secure Gate Access Control System. Perform the following validations and generate a detailed launch checklist:\n\n## Core User Journey Validation\n1. **Authentication Flows**: Test login, logout, token refresh, MFA setup for all user roles (admin, guard, resident)\n2. **Visitor Management**: End-to-end visitor invitation, approval, check-in/check-out flows\n3. **Critical API Endpoints**: Verify all essential APIs are functional with proper error handling\n4. **Route Protection**: Confirm role-based access control works across all protected routes\n5. **Real-time Features**: Test WebSocket connections, live updates, notifications\n\n## Specification Completeness\n1. **Requirements Coverage**: Verify all user stories and acceptance criteria are implemented\n2. **Design Consistency**: Check UI/UX matches design specifications and accessibility standards\n3. **Task Completion**: Confirm all development tasks are complete with proper documentation\n4. **API Documentation**: Validate API docs match actual implementation\n\n## Test Coverage & Quality\n1. **Unit Tests**: Check test coverage on critical business logic (>80% target)\n2. **Integration Tests**: Verify API endpoint tests cover happy path and error scenarios\n3. **E2E Tests**: Confirm end-to-end user journey tests are passing\n4. **Security Tests**: Validate authentication, authorization, and input validation tests\n\n## Database & Migration Safety\n1. **Migration Scripts**: Review all pending migrations for safety and rollback compatibility\n2. **Data Integrity**: Verify foreign key constraints and data validation rules\n3. **Backup Strategy**: Confirm backup procedures and recovery testing\n4. **Performance**: Check query performance and indexing strategy\n\n## Observability & Monitoring\n1. **Logging**: Verify structured logging is implemented with appropriate levels\n2. **Error Tracking**: Confirm Sentry integration and error reporting\n3. **Health Endpoints**: Test /health, /health/detailed, and monitoring endpoints\n4. **Metrics Collection**: Validate performance and business metrics tracking\n5. **Alerting**: Check alert configuration for critical system events\n\n## Deployment Readiness\n1. **Netlify Frontend**:\n   - Build process succeeds without errors\n   - Environment variables properly configured\n   - Static asset optimization and CDN setup\n   - SSL certificate and domain configuration\n\n2. **Render Backend**:\n   - Service starts successfully\n   - Database connection established\n   - Health checks passing\n   - Environment secrets properly configured\n   - Auto-scaling and resource limits set\n\n3. **External Services**:\n   - Email service (Mailgun) configuration and testing\n   - SMS service (AfricaTalking) integration verification\n   - Redis session store connectivity\n   - Third-party API integrations\n\n## Security Validation\n1. **Authentication Security**: JWT implementation, token rotation, session management\n2. **Authorization**: Role-based access control and estate scoping\n3. **Input Validation**: SQL injection, XSS, and CSRF protection\n4. **Security Headers**: CSP, HSTS, and other security headers configured\n5. **Secrets Management**: Proper handling of API keys and sensitive data\n\n## Performance Validation\n1. **Load Testing**: Basic load testing on critical endpoints\n2. **Database Performance**: Query optimization and connection pooling\n3. **Caching Strategy**: Redis caching and CDN configuration\n4. **Resource Usage**: Memory and CPU usage under normal load\n\nGenerate a comprehensive launch checklist with:\n- ✅ for fully ready items\n- ⚠️ for items with minor issues or recommendations\n- ❌ for critical blockers that must be fixed\n\nFor each item, provide:\n- Current status and findings\n- Specific issues identified (if any)\n- Recommended fixes or improvements\n- Priority level (Critical/High/Medium/Low)\n\nInclude a final recommendation on launch readiness and a prioritized list of any remaining blockers that must be addressed before production deployment."
  }
}